message: >-
  If you use this protocol, its circuits, or this code, please cite both the
  software (this entry) and the paper (preferred-citation, below).
type: software
title: "Proof of Personhood Without a Registry"
abstract: >-
  A measured zero-knowledge construction for one-human-one-action gating with no
  central registry, no biometrics, and no hardware root of trust. Enrolment
  proves k independent attestations once; every later login proves set membership
  in a published Poseidon Merkle tree plus a per-context rate-limiting-nullifier
  share, in a 4,309-constraint Groth16/BN254 circuit. The repository carries the
  reference implementation, the circuits, an OIDC / W3C Verifiable Presentation
  integration, reproducible builds, an adversarial self-audit that includes a
  tool-independent two-witness under-constraint search, and the raw on-device
  measurements.
